 sustain 3,200 contacts per hour for six hours. Forecast demand is 4,100 per hour unless alternate-language outreach reduces repeat calls.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCIPHER and AURORA determine advisory status; INDIGO and BASTION supply service observations. HELIX constrains publication of sensitive infrastructure details.\nJASPER supplies mandatory environmental language and KESTREL supplies verified alternate-water locations.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| COM-000 | sms | v2 | 91.0 | percent-delivered | superseded |\n| COM-001 | radio | v2 | 92.3 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-002 | clinics | v2 | 93.6 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-003 | schools | v2 | 91.8 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-004 | sms | v2 | 93.1 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-005 | radio | v2 | 91.3 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-006 | clinics | v2 | 92.6 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-007 | schools | v2 | 93.9 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-008 | sms | v2 | 92.1 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-009 | radio | v2 | 93.4 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-010 | clinics | v2 | 91.6 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-011 | schools | v2 | 92.9 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-012 | sms | v2 | 91.1 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-013 | radio | v2 | 92.4 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-014 | clinics | v3 | 93.7 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-015 | schools | v3 | 91.9 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-016 | sms | v3 | 93.2 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-017 | radio | v3 | 91.4 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-018 | clinics | v3 | 92.7 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-019 | schools | v3 | 94.0 | percent-delivered | superseded |\n| COM-020 | sms | v3 | 92.2 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-021 | radio | v3 | 93.5 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-022 | clinics | v3 | 91.7 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-023 | schools | v3 | 93.0 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-024 | sms | v3 | 91.2 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-025 | radio | v3 | 92.5 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-026 | clinics | v3 | 93.8 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-027 | schools | v3 | 92.0 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-028 | sms | v4 | 93.3 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-029 | radio | v4 | 91.5 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-030 | clinics | v4 | 92.8 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-031 | schools | v4 | 91.0 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-032 | sms | v4 | 92.3 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-033 | radio | v4 | 93.6 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-034 | clinics | v4 | 91.8 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-035 | schools | v4 | 93.1 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-036 | sms | v4 | 91.3 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-037 | radio | v4 | 92.6 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-038 | clinics | v4 | 93.9 | percent-delivered | superseded |\n| COM-039 | schools | v4 | 92.1 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-040 | sms | v4 | 93.4 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-041 | radio | v4 | 91.6 | percent-delivered | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve delivery coverage, state vocabulary, capacity, forecast, accessibility, and privacy.\nState owners, channels, timing, acknowledgments, alternates, and retirement evidence.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"MOSAIC\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"NEXUS\",\"start_line\":1}]\n}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:MOSAIC:1-64+NEXUS:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"ce0798821f875aeea4f1794555e0c92c53cc571a95cfecafa85dbd7dfc319fc1\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-007\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"MOSAIC\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"NEXUS\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8078}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"MOSAIC\",\"source_path\":\"sources/MOSAIC_CHANGE.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"a3836321537dc4f3ee3cacc094761d5176c0a7f08ae891f4fc4e1ee5b3f84b4d\",\"source_size_bytes\":3861,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Candidate lineage, rollback, and configuration control\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe current recovery candidate is W7 with hydraulic model H12, pump plan P9, treatment plan T6, and key set W4. Evidence for W6 is historical unless explicitly transferred and rechecked.\nRollback to W6 is mechanically possible only while valve map V8 and controller firmware C11 remain compatible. Mechanical possibility is not authorization.\nEvery mutation must record before and after candidate hashes, changed files, affected evidence, check currency, owner, and rollback effect.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nBASTION, CIPHER, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON, and HELIX observations can become stale after MOSAIC candidate changes.\nNEXUS reviews current-candidate evidence independently; AURORA authorizes execution and closure separately.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| CHG-000 | hydraulic-model | v2 | 7.0 | candidate-index | superseded |\n| CHG-001 | pump-plan | v2 | 8.3 | candidate-index | current |\n| CHG-002 | treatment-plan | v2 | 9.6 | candidate-index | current |\n| CHG-003 | key-set | v2 | 7.8 | candidate-index | current |\n| CHG-004 | hydraulic-model | v2 | 9.1 | candidate-index | current |\n| CHG-005 | pump-plan | v2 | 7.3 | candidate-index | current |\n| CHG-006 | treatment-plan | v2 | 8.6 | candidate-index | current |\n| CHG-007 | key-set | v2 | 9.9 | candidate-index | current |\n| CHG-008 | hydraulic-model | v2 | 8.1 | candidate-index | current |\n| CHG-009 | pump-plan | v2 |