"sources/NEXUS_READINESS.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"85aabce45a9704e4f55ee1418528eb083a7c46326dbb366b0cb4a3ddcd9df0d6\",\"source_size_bytes\":3762,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Independent readiness review, blockers, and falsifiers\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe latest independent review found sixteen open findings: five hydraulic, four treatment, three sampling, two power, and two communication. A finding count is not a readiness percentage.\nBlocking findings include incomplete second-round samples, stale generator transfer evidence, and missing acknowledgment from the public-health duty officer.\nReadiness requires current candidate-bound evidence for every blocking control, independent review of residual risk, and explicit acceptance by the authorized owner.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nNEXUS consumes evidence from AURORA, BASTION, CIPHER, ECHO, FALCON, HELIX, INDIGO, LUMEN, and MOSAIC but does not mutate their states.\nAn artifact, semantic register, mechanical check, or submission proposal cannot self-authorize readiness.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| RDY-000 | hydraulic | v2 | 16.0 | open-findings | superseded |\n| RDY-001 | quality | v2 | 17.3 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-002 | power | v2 | 18.6 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-003 | public-health | v2 | 16.8 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-004 | hydraulic | v2 | 18.1 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-005 | quality | v2 | 16.3 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-006 | power | v2 | 17.6 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-007 | public-health | v2 | 18.9 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-008 | hydraulic | v2 | 17.1 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-009 | quality | v2 | 18.4 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-010 | power | v2 | 16.6 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-011 | public-health | v2 | 17.9 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-012 | hydraulic | v2 | 16.1 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-013 | quality | v2 | 17.4 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-014 | power | v3 | 18.7 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-015 | public-health | v3 | 16.9 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-016 | hydraulic | v3 | 18.2 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-017 | quality | v3 | 16.4 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-018 | power | v3 | 17.7 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-019 | public-health | v3 | 19.0 | open-findings | superseded |\n| RDY-020 | hydraulic | v3 | 17.2 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-021 | quality | v3 | 18.5 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-022 | power | v3 | 16.7 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-023 | public-health | v3 | 18.0 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-024 | hydraulic | v3 | 16.2 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-025 | quality | v3 | 17.5 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-026 | power | v3 | 18.8 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-027 | public-health | v3 | 17.0 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-028 | hydraulic | v4 | 18.3 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-029 | quality | v4 | 16.5 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-030 | power | v4 | 17.8 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-031 | public-health | v4 | 16.0 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-032 | hydraulic | v4 | 17.3 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-033 | quality | v4 | 18.6 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-034 | power | v4 | 16.8 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-035 | public-health | v4 | 18.1 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-036 | hydraulic | v4 | 16.3 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-037 | quality | v4 | 17.6 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-038 | power | v4 | 18.9 | open-findings | superseded |\n| RDY-039 | public-health | v4 | 17.1 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-040 | hydraulic | v4 | 18.4 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-041 | quality | v4 | 16.6 | open-findings | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nList blockers, falsifiers, residual risks, owners, current evidence, and acceptance.\nKeep independent review separate from execution, communication, and closure authority.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"replace_evidence_ledger\",\"content\":\"# Solace Evidence and Decision Matrix\\n\\n| ID | Source | Fact/Constraint | Unit/Status | Dependencies/Conflicts | Unknowns/Currency | Citation |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| AUR-01 | AURORA | Emergency restoration authority separated from public-health and communication closure authority. | Authority / Current | Binds NEXUS review, JASPER materiality, LUMEN advisory state. | Owner acceptance required for closure; stale if role-policy mutates. | [AURORA] |\\n| BAS-01 | BASTION | Hydraulic pressure, storage, isolation, residence time, and candidate-bound hydraulics govern zone control. | Pressure/Volume / Current | Isolates zones when triggers met; depends on INDIGO telemetry currency. | Stale if valve map V8 or controller firmware C11 changes. | [BASTION] |\\n| CIP-01 | CIPHER | Sampling rounds, spacing, detection limits, action thresholds, and staleness define clearance evidence. | Conc/Limit / Current | Must sample each materially different source path per GARNET. | Second-round samples incomplete; stale if source-water blend changes. | [CIPHER] |\\n| DEL-01 | DELTA | Pump capacity, shared-main limits, staged demand, and cavitation constraints bound flow restoration. | Flow/Head / Current | Competes with FALCON for ECHO capacity; depends on KESTREL staffing. | Stale if pump plan P9 or demand ramp changes. | [DELTA] |\\n| ECH-01 | ECHO | Grid rated 8.2 MW, usable 6.5 MW; generator 4.1 MW for 36 hours at current fuel. | Power/Duration / Current | Transfer drill stale for switchgear SW-9; KESTREL fuel controls duration. | Usable vs rated power must not swap; stale if switchgear version changes. | [ECHO] |\\n| FAL-01 | FALCON | Turbidity 0.18 NTU (gate ≤0.30 NTU for 4h); Cl₂ 0.8–2.0 mg/L entry, ≥0.2 mg/L distribution. | NTU/mg/L / Current | Contact time, UV, and source blend changes stale prior verification. | Entry vs distribution thresholds distinct; stale if treatment plan T6 changes. | [FALCON] |\\n| GAR-01 | GARNET | Ash-plume 34% forecast (not measured) intake impact; VOC non-detect reservoir, 3.1 µg/L river intake. | %/µg/L / Current | Investigation hold active for chemical yard (trench uninspected). | Forecast vs observation distinct; stale if rain event or inspection occurs. | [GARNET] |\\n| HEL-01 | HELIX | SCADA token revoked 14:10 UTC; controller key current under W4; break-glass expires in 2h with dual approval. | Time/Key / Current | Immutable logging required; retention 90d online, 7y incident. | Remote automation restoration requires named evidence; stale if key-set mutates. | [HELIX] |\\n| IND-01 | INDIGO | Critical-signal coverage 96%; pressure warning 38 psi, isolation trigger 30 psi; delay p95 700ms, p99 1200ms. | %/Psi/ms / Current | Coverage ≠ confidence; warnings vs actions distinct. | Uninstrumented zones unproven; stale if telemetry config changes. | [INDIGO] |\\n| JAS-01 | JASPER | Material unauthorized discharge notice within 72h of determination; dechlorination residual >0.019 mg/L at outfall stops discharge. | Hours/mg/L / Current | Permit E-17 governs emergency dechlorination; 7y retention with provenance. | Determination event unknown until AURORA materiality decision. | [JASPER] |\\n| KES-01 | KESTREL | Diesel 36h emergency load, 22h full pump load; coagulant 4.5d, chlorine 3.2d; 6 operators at 06:00 UTC ±90min. | Hours/Days / Current | Fuel controls ECHO duration; chemicals control FALCON staging. | Inventory ≠ delivery lead time; stale if consumption regime changes. | [KESTREL] |\\n| LUM-01 | LUMEN | Do-not-drink reached 91% endpoints; call center 3,200/hr for 6h vs forecast 4,100/hr. | %/Contacts / Current | States: do-not-use, do-not-drink, boil-water, restricted, cleared. | Low pressure ≠ contamination; stale if advisory status changes. | [LUMEN] |\\n| MOS-01 | MOSAIC | Current candidate W7 (H12, P9, T6, W4); rollback to W6 requires V8/C11 compatibility. | Version / Current | Every mutation records before/after hashes, files, effects, checks. | Mechanical possibility ≠ authorization; stale if any component mutates. | [MOSAIC] |\\n| NEX-01 | NEXUS | 16 open findings (5 hydraulic, 4 treatment, 3 sampling, 2 power, 2 comm); blockers: samples, generator transfer, PHO acknowledgment. | Findings / Current | Independent review separate from execution; no self-authorization. | Residual risk acceptance required; stale if blocking controls change. | [NEXUS] |\\n\\n## Cross-Source Dependencies & Staleness Triggers\\n\\n- **Hydraulics**: BASTION isolation depends on INDIGO pressure triggers (30 psi action vs 38 psi warning) and MOSAIC candidate W7 currency.\\n- **Treatment**: FALCON verification stale if GARNET source blend, BASTION residence time, CIPHER sampling, or DELTA demand ramps change.\\n- **Power**: ECHO generator duration controlled by KESTREL fuel stock; transfer evidence stale for switchgear SW-9.\\n- **Security**: HELIX remote automation requires current key-set W4, immutable logging, and AURORA authorization; stale if role-policy mutates.\\n- **Environmental**: JASPER 72h notice clock starts at AURORA materiality determination, not detection; dechlorination stop threshold 0.019 mg/L.\\n- **Readiness**: NEXUS blocking findings (samples, generator transfer, PHO acknowledgment) must be resolved with current candidate-bound evidence before independent readiness acceptance.\\n\\n## Unit & Threshold Preservation Rules\\n\\n- Psi ≠ kPa; gallons ≠ treated reserve; µg/L ≠ mg/L; reporting limit ≠ action threshold.\\n- Percentage coverage ≠ confidence; rated power ≠ usable power; nameplate capacity ≠ shared capacity.\\n- Warning threshold (38 psi) ≠ isolation trigger (30 psi); forecast probability (34%) ≠ measured concentration.\\n- Mechanical checks ≠ public-health readiness ≠ independent acceptance.\\n\\n## Candidate Currency & Blockers\\n\\n- Current candidate: W7 (H12, P9, T6, W4).\\n- Blocking findings: incomplete second-round samples [CIPHER], stale generator transfer evidence [ECHO], missing PHO acknowledgment [AURORA/NEXUS].\\n- Investigation hold: chemical yard trench uninspected [GARNET].\\n- Rollback to W6 mechanically possible only while V8/C11 compatible; not authorized.\\n\\n## Falsifiers for Important Claims\\n\\n- If turbidity exceeds 0.30 NTU for 4h, treatment verification falsified [FALCON].\\n- If Cl₂ residual <0.8 mg/L at entry or <0.2 mg/L in distribution, disinfection claim falsified [FALCON].\\n- If pressure drops below 30 psi, isolation trigger activated; warning-only claims falsified [INDIGO/BASTION].\\n- If VOC detected at reservoir (currently non-detect), source-path separation falsified [GARNET].\\n- If generator transfer fails under SW-9, continuity claim falsified [ECHO].\\n- If dechlorination residual >0.019 mg/L at outfall, permit compliance falsified [JASPER].\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"candidate:EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md\",\"object_version\":\"candidate-v001:232e4f81cdac6c04341630d4c5b02c31e578201e6441822eda1f2b802d10f148\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-008\",\"result_kind\":\"candidate_effect\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"after_sha256\":\"232e4f81cdac6c04341630d4c5b02c31e578201e6441822eda1f2b802d10f148\",\"before_sha256\":\"9a228857dd50e69921af6d67c22e74bd3156dfb6266475ce63838881a822da61\",\"candidate_version\":\"candidate-v001:232e4f81cdac6c04341630d4c5b02c31e578201e6441822eda1f2b802d10f148\",\"cause\":\"actor_replace_evidence_ledger\",\"changed_file\":\"EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md\",\"current_candidate_verification_status\":\"not_run_after_candidate_effect\",\"prior_check_binding\":null,\"schema\":\"architecture-candidate-effect-v0\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"result:RESULT-001\",\"object_version\":\"58d3d2717469174d7313108815f4c33d7b2b8d28dcf690f6e964c8ad23db7386\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-009\",\"result_kind\":\"exact_reopen_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"original_result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"original_sha256\":\"58d3d2717469174d7313108815f4c33d7b2b8d28dcf690f6e964c8ad23db7386\",\"schema\":\"architecture-exact-reopen-v0\"}\n--- exact original model-visible result ---\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:AURORA:1-64+BASTION:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"d40538a3737a4f373b7eabc2e3a41e0637476655cf7441bd9c309545cffc2f71\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"AURORA\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8057}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"AURORA\",\"source_path\":\"sources/AURORA_AUTHORITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"debbe3de17dc0511fe3b9f5be920a83367c84efaedb34ef4095a9add315a0761\",\"source_size_bytes\":4111,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Emergency authority and restoration accountability\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe incident commander may isolate zones and order emergency work. Only the county health officer may lift a do-not-drink order, and only after current laboratory and distribution-system verification; a utility repair or green mechanical check is not public-health authorization.\nEmergency procurement does not waive operator certification, chain of custody, environmental permits, access control, or fiscal review. Final closure requires the utility director to accept every declared blocker and residual risk.\nA handoff is valid only when the receiving lead acknowledges the same hydraulic model, treatment train, sampling plan, pump configuration, and communication version. A version mismatch blocks closure.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nBASTION and CIPHER supply hydraulic and laboratory evidence but cannot lift health restrictions. NEXUS supplies independent readiness findings but does not execute restoration.\nMOSAIC owns rollback mechanics; AURORA preserves separation among detection, recommendation, authorization, execution, verification, communication, and closure.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| AUT-000 | incident-command | v2 | 1.0 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-001 | health-officer | v2 | 2.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-002 | utility-director | v2 | 3.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-003 | public-information | v2 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-004 | incident-command | v2 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-005 | health-officer | v2 | 1.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-006 | utility-director | v2 | 2.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-007 | public-information | v2 | 3.9 | approval | current |\n| AUT-008 | incident-command | v2 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-009 | health-officer | v2 | 3.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-010 | utility-director | v2 | 1.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-011 | public-information | v2 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n| AUT-012 | incident-command | v2 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-013 | health-officer | v2 | 2.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-014 | utility-director | v3 | 3.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-015 | public-information | v3 | 1.9 | approval | current |\n| AUT-016 | incident-command | v3 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-017 | health-officer | v3 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-018 | utility-director | v3 | 2.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-019 | public-information | v3 | 4.0 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-020 | incident-command | v3 | 2.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-021 | health-officer | v3 | 3.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-022 | utility-director | v3 | 1.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-023 | public-information | v3 | 3.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-024 | incident-command | v3 | 1.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-025 | health-officer | v3 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-026 | utility-director | v3 | 3.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-027 | public-information | v3 | 2.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-028 | incident-command | v4 | 3.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-029 | health-officer | v4 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-030 | utility-director | v4 | 2.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-031 | public-information | v4 | 1.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-032 | incident-command | v4 | 2.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-033 | health-officer | v4 | 3.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-034 | utility-director | v4 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-035 | public-information | v4 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-036 | incident-command | v4 | 1.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-037 | health-officer | v4 | 2.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-038 | utility-director | v4 | 3.9 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-039 | public-information | v4 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-040 | incident-command | v4 | 3.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-041 | health-officer | v4 | 1.6 | approval | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nName who may isolate, repair, verify, reopen service, lift advisories, and close.\nTreat semantic records and candidate mutations as non-authoritative work products.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"source_path\":\"sources/BASTION_HYDRAULICS.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"f0a85d8273e5058984554a6383d51616f2e103f141b7e268f67215b90fc7ed60\",\"source_size_bytes\":3483,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Hydraulic pressure, storage, and zone isolation evidence\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nCurrent minimum distribution pressure is 42 psi in the north zone. The restoration gate is at least 35 psi at every critical node for three consecutive thirty-minute windows; 42 psi must not be converted to 42 kPa or treated as proof of water quality.\nRidge storage contains 5.8 million gallons, while the twelve-hour emergency reserve is 3.2 million gallons. Stored volume and usable treated reserve are different controls.\nA valve map, pump curve, demand allocation, or zone-boundary change makes earlier pressure and residence-time checks stale for the changed candidate.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nDELTA pump sequencing depends on BASTION pressure and ECHO power. CIPHER sampling locations must follow the current BASTION flow paths.\nMOSAIC rollback is allowed only while the prior valve map remains valid and a current BASTION pressure check passes for the rollback candidate.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| HYD-000 | north-zone | v2 | 42.0 | psi | superseded |\n| HYD-001 | south-zone | v2 | 43.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-002 | ridge-tank | v2 | 44.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-003 | valve-grid | v2 | 42.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-004 | north-zone | v2 | 44.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-005 | south-zone | v2 | 42.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-006 | ridge-tank | v2 | 43.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-007 | valve-grid | v2 | 44.9 | psi | current |\n| HYD-008 | north-zone | v2 | 43.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-009 | south-zone | v2 | 44.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-010 | ridge-tank | v2 | 42.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-011 | valve-grid | v2 | 43.9 | psi | current |\n| HYD-012 | north-zone | v2 | 42.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-013 | south-zone | v2 | 43.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-014 | ridge-tank | v3 | 44.7 | psi | current |\n| HYD-015 | valve-grid | v3 | 42.9 | psi | current |\n| HYD-016 | north-zone | v3 | 44.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-017 | south-zone | v3 | 42.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-018 | ridge-tank | v3 | 43.7 | psi | current |\n| HYD-019 | valve-grid | v3 | 45.0 | psi | superseded |\n| HYD-020 | north-zone | v3 | 43.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-021 | south-zone | v3 | 44.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-022 | ridge-tank | v3 | 42.7 | psi | current |\n| HYD-023 | valve-grid | v3 | 44.0 | psi | current |\n| HYD-024 | north-zone | v3 | 42.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-025 | south-zone | v3 | 43.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-026 | ridge-tank | v3 | 44.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-027 | valve-grid | v3 | 43.0 | psi | current |\n| HYD-028 | north-zone | v4 | 44.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-029 | south-zone | v4 | 42.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-030 | ridge-tank | v4 | 43.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-031 | valve-grid | v4 | 42.0 | psi | current |\n| HYD-032 | north-zone | v4 | 43.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-033 | south-zone | v4 | 44.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-034 | ridge-tank | v4 | 42.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-035 | valve-grid | v4 | 44.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-036 | north-zone | v4 | 42.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-037 | south-zone | v4 | 43.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-038 | ridge-tank | v4 | 44.9 | psi | superseded |\n| HYD-039 | valve-grid | v4 | 43.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-040 | north-zone | v4 | 44.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-041 | south-zone | v4 | 42.6 | psi | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve psi, gallons, the three-window rule, and candidate currency.\nDistinguish hydraulic service from microbiological and chemical clearance.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-002\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"result:RESULT-002\",\"object_version\":\"ff48adcd9a8685c9568506e43f953213d7d1728c2b4ca22b125cbc7d3e0dbcc7\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-010\",\"result_kind\":\"exact_reopen_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"original_result_id\":\"RESULT-002\",\"original_sha256\":\"ff48adcd9a8685c9568506e43f953213d7d1728c2b4ca22b125cbc7d3e0dbcc7\",\"schema\":\"architecture-exact-reopen-v0\"}\n--- exact original model-visible result ---\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:CIPHER:1-64+DELTA:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"64721c48b86decba9adecca404e0e207db15cc1c0611470f2fe6e28207610bef\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-002\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8452}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"source_path\":\"sources/CIPHER_LAB.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"6db7f6a91d666ab9e013e147aa946885080f48117bd461c8a542171378aba4cb\",\"source_size_bytes\":3991,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Laboratory sampling, detection limits, and clearance evidence\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe current confirmatory set has zero E. coli positives across forty-eight samples. Clearance requires two complete rounds at least sixteen hours apart; one clean round is insufficient.\nThe benzene reporting limit is 0.5 micrograms per liter and the action threshold is 5.0 micrograms per liter. The reporting limit is not the action threshold and neither is a percent concentration.\nA flow-path, disinfectant-dose, source-water, sampling-plan, or laboratory-method change makes prior samples stale for the changed candidate.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCIPHER sample placement consumes BASTION flow paths and GARNET contamination hypotheses. HELIX governs chain of custody and laboratory access.\nAURORA consumes current CIPHER findings for advisory decisions; CIPHER does not itself authorize public restoration.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| LAB-000 | entry-point | v2 | 0.0 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-001 | north-grid | v2 | 1.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-002 | south-grid | v2 | 2.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-003 | hospital-loop | v2 | 0.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-004 | entry-point | v2 | 2.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-005 | north-grid | v2 | 0.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-006 | south-grid | v2 | 1.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-007 | hospital-loop | v2 | 2.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-008 | entry-point | v2 | 1.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-009 | north-grid | v2 | 2.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-010 | south-grid | v2 | 0.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-011 | hospital-loop | v2 | 1.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-012 | entry-point | v2 | 0.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-013 | north-grid | v2 | 1.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-014 | south-grid | v3 | 2.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-015 | hospital-loop | v3 | 0.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-016 | entry-point | v3 | 2.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-017 | north-grid | v3 | 0.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-018 | south-grid | v3 | 1.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-019 | hospital-loop | v3 | 3.0 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-020 | entry-point | v3 | 1.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-021 | north-grid | v3 | 2.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-022 | south-grid | v3 | 0.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-023 | hospital-loop | v3 | 2.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-024 | entry-point | v3 | 0.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-025 | north-grid | v3 | 1.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-026 | south-grid | v3 | 2.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-027 | hospital-loop | v3 | 1.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-028 | entry-point | v4 | 2.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-029 | north-grid | v4 | 0.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-030 | south-grid | v4 | 1.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-031 | hospital-loop | v4 | 0.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-032 | entry-point | v4 | 1.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-033 | north-grid | v4 | 2.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-034 | south-grid | v4 | 0.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-035 | hospital-loop | v4 | 2.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-036 | entry-point | v4 | 0.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-037 | north-grid | v4 | 1.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-038 | south-grid | v4 | 2.9 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-039 | hospital-loop | v4 | 1.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-040 | entry-point | v4 | 2.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-041 | north-grid | v4 | 0.6 | positive-samples | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve rounds, spacing, sample count, detection limit, action threshold, and staleness.\nState what negative result would falsify clearance and trigger renewed isolation.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"source_path\":\"sources/DELTA_PUMPS.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"4c3707d0d2ae07ceb2bda6d83cf6585510f5398db7c66568ba38aa3fd3f01169\",\"source_size_bytes\":4013,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Pump capacity, sequencing, and cavitation constraints\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe treatment works can supply 18 million gallons per day, but the shared transmission main is capped at 14.5 MGD. Pump nameplate capacities cannot be summed into usable system flow.\nThe latest inspected configuration sustained 12.8 MGD after fire-flow and hospital reserve. A higher stage requires a current candidate-bound pump and pressure test.\nRestoration may advance through 10, 30, 60, and 100 percent demand stages only after two thirty-minute windows meet pressure, turbidity, power, and storage gates.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nBASTION supplies pressure limits, ECHO supplies feeder headroom, and FALCON supplies treatment output. All three constrain DELTA sequencing.\nA pump, valve, main allocation, generator, or treatment-train change makes prior capacity evidence stale.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| PMP-000 | pump-1 | v2 | 18.0 | million-gallons-day | superseded |\n| PMP-001 | pump-2 | v2 | 19.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-002 | booster-east | v2 | 20.6 | million-gallons-day | current 