| superseded |\n| RDY-039 | public-health | v4 | 17.1 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-040 | hydraulic | v4 | 18.4 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-041 | quality | v4 | 16.6 | open-findings | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nList blockers, falsifiers, residual risks, owners, current evidence, and acceptance.\nKeep independent review separate from execution, communication, and closure authority.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"replace_evidence_ledger\",\"content\":\"# Solace Evidence and Decision Matrix\\n\\n| ID | Source | Fact/Constraint | Unit/Status | Dependencies/Conflicts | Unknowns/Currency | Citation |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| AUR-01 | AURORA | Emergency restoration authority separated from public-health and communication closure authority. | Authority / Current | Binds NEXUS review, JASPER materiality, LUMEN advisory state. | Owner acceptance required for closure; stale if role-policy mutates. | [AURORA] |\\n| BAS-01 | BASTION | Hydraulic pressure, storage, isolation, residence time, and candidate-bound hydraulics govern zone control. | Pressure/Volume / Current | Isolates zones when triggers met; depends on INDIGO telemetry currency. | Stale if valve map V8 or controller firmware C11 changes. | [BASTION] |\\n| CIP-01 | CIPHER | Sampling rounds, spacing, detection limits, action thresholds, and staleness define clearance evidence. | Conc/Limit / Current | Must sample each materially different source path per GARNET. | Second-round samples incomplete; stale if source-water blend changes. | [CIPHER] |\\n| DEL-01 | DELTA | Pump capacity, shared-main limits, staged demand, and cavitation constraints bound flow restoration. | Flow/Head / Current | Competes with FALCON for ECHO capacity; depends on KESTREL staffing. | Stale if pump plan P9 or demand ramp changes. | [DELTA] |\\n| ECH-01 | ECHO | Grid rated 8.2 MW, usable 6.5 MW; generator 4.1 MW for 36 hours at current fuel. | Power/Duration / Current | Transfer drill stale for switchgear SW-9; KESTREL fuel controls duration. | Usable vs rated power must not swap; stale if switchgear version changes. | [ECHO] |\\n| FAL-01 | FALCON | Turbidity 0.18 NTU (gate ≤0.30 NTU for 4h); Cl₂ 0.8–2.0 mg/L entry, ≥0.2 mg/L distribution. | NTU/mg/L / Current | Contact time, UV, and source blend changes stale prior verification. | Entry vs distribution thresholds distinct; stale if treatment plan T6 changes. | [FALCON] |\\n| GAR-01 | GARNET | Ash-plume 34% forecast (not measured) intake impact; VOC non-detect reservoir, 3.1 µg/L river intake. | %/µg/L / Current | Investigation hold active for chemical yard (trench uninspected). | Forecast vs observation distinct; stale if rain event or inspection occurs. | [GARNET] |\\n| HEL-01 | HELIX | SCADA token revoked 14:10 UTC; controller key current under W4; break-glass expires in 2h with dual approval. | Time/Key / Current | Immutable logging required; retention 90d online, 7y incident. | Remote automation restoration requires named evidence; stale if key-set mutates. | [HELIX] |\\n| IND-01 | INDIGO | Critical-signal coverage 96%; pressure warning 38 psi, isolation trigger 30 psi; delay p95 700ms, p99 1200ms. | %/Psi/ms / Current | Coverage ≠ confidence; warnings vs actions distinct. | Uninstrumented zones unproven; stale if telemetry config changes. | [INDIGO] |\\n| JAS-01 | JASPER | Material unauthorized discharge notice within 72h of determination; dechlorination residual >0.019 mg/L at outfall stops discharge. | Hours/mg/L / Current | Permit E-17 governs emergency dechlorination; 7y retention with provenance. | Determination event unknown until AURORA materiality decision. | [JASPER] |\\n| KES-01 | KESTREL | Diesel 36h emergency load, 22h full pump load; coagulant 4.5d, chlorine 3.2d; 6 operators at 06:00 UTC ±90min. | Hours/Days / Current | Fuel controls ECHO duration; chemicals control FALCON staging. | Inventory ≠ delivery lead time; stale if consumption regime changes. | [KESTREL] |\\n| LUM-01 | LUMEN | Do-not-drink reached 91% endpoints; call center 3,200/hr for 6h vs forecast 4,100/hr. | %/Contacts / Current | States: do-not-use, do-not-drink, boil-water, restricted, cleared. | Low pressure ≠ contamination; stale if advisory status changes. | [LUMEN] |\\n| MOS-01 | MOSAIC | Current candidate W7 (H12, P9, T6, W4); rollback to W6 requires V8/C11 compatibility. | Version / Current | Every mutation records before/after hashes, files, effects, checks. | Mechanical possibility ≠ authorization; stale if any component mutates. | [MOSAIC] |\\n| NEX-01 | NEXUS | 16 open findings (5 hydraulic, 4 treatment, 3 sampling, 2 power, 2 comm); blockers: samples, generator transfer, PHO acknowledgment. | Findings / Current | Independent review separate from execution; no self-authorization. | Residual risk acceptance required; stale if blocking controls change. | [NEXUS] |\\n\\n## Cross-Source Dependencies & Staleness Triggers\\n\\n- **Hydraulics**: BASTION isolation depends on INDIGO pressure triggers (30 psi action vs 38 psi warning) and MOSAIC candidate W7 currency.\\n- **Treatment**: FALCON verification stale if GARNET source blend, BASTION residence time, CIPHER sampling, or DELTA demand ramps change.\\n- **Power**: ECHO generator duration controlled by KESTREL fuel stock; transfer evidence stale for switchgear SW-9.\\n- **Security**: HELIX remote automation requires current key-set W4, immutable logging, and AURORA authorization; stale if role-policy mutates.\\n- **Environmental**: JASPER 72h notice clock starts at AURORA materiality determination, not detection; dechlorination stop threshold 0.019 mg/L.\\n- **Readiness**: NEXUS blocking findings (samples, generator transfer, PHO acknowledgment) must be resolved with current candidate-bound evidence before independent readiness acceptance.\\n\\n## Unit & Threshold Preservation Rules\\n\\n- Psi ≠ kPa; gallons ≠ treated reserve; µg/L ≠ mg/L; reporting limit ≠ action threshold.\\n- Percentage coverage ≠ confidence; rated power ≠ usable power; nameplate capacity ≠ shared capacity.\\n- Warning threshold (38 psi) ≠ isolation trigger (30 psi); forecast probability (34%) ≠ measured concentration.\\n- Mechanical checks ≠ public-health readiness ≠ independent acceptance.\\n\\n## Candidate Currency & Blockers\\n\\n- Current candidate: W7 (H12, P9, T6, W4).\\n- Blocking findings: incomplete second-round samples [CIPHER], stale generator transfer evidence [ECHO], missing PHO acknowledgment [AURORA/NEXUS].\\n- Investigation hold: chemical yard trench uninspected [GARNET].\\n- Rollback to W6 mechanically possible only while V8/C11 compatible; not authorized.\\n\\n## Falsifiers for Important Claims\\n\\n- If turbidity exceeds 0.30 NTU for 4h, treatment verification falsified [FALCON].\\n- If Cl₂ residual <0.8 mg/L at entry or <0.2 mg/L in distribution, disinfection claim falsified [FALCON].\\n- If pressure drops below 30 psi, isolation trigger activated; warning-only claims falsified [INDIGO/BASTION].\\n- If VOC detected at reservoir (currently non-detect), source-path separation falsified [GARNET].\\n- If generator transfer fails under SW-9, continuity claim falsified [ECHO].\\n- If dechlorination residual >0.019 mg/L at outfall, permit compliance falsified [JASPER].\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"candidate:EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md\",\"object_version\":\"candidate-v001:232e4f81cdac6c04341630d4c5b02c31e578201e6441822eda1f2b802d10f148\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-008\",\"result_kind\":\"candidate_effect\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"after_sha256\":\"232e4f81cdac6c04341630d4c5b02c31e578201e6441822eda1f2b802d10f148\",\"before_sha256\":\"9a228857dd50e69921af6d67c22e74bd3156dfb6266475ce63838881a822da61\",\"candidate_version\":\"candidate-v001:232e4f81cdac6c04341630d4c5b02c31e578201e6441822eda1f2b802d10f148\",\"cause\":\"actor_replace_evidence_ledger\",\"changed_file\":\"EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md\",\"current_candidate_verification_status\":\"not_run_after_candidate_effect\",\"prior_check_binding\":null,\"schema\":\"architecture-candidate-effect-v0\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"result:RESULT-001\",\"object_version\":\"58d3d2717469174d7313108815f4c33d7b2b8d28dcf690f6e964c8ad23db7386\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-009\",\"result_kind\":\"exact_reopen_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"original_result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"original_sha256\":\"58d3d2717469174d7313108815f4c33d7b2b8d28dcf690f6e964c8ad23db7386\",\"schema\":\"architecture-exact-reopen-v0\"}\n--- exact original model-visible result ---\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:AURORA:1-64+BASTION:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"d40538a3737a4f373b7eabc2e3a41e0637476655cf7441bd9c309545cffc2f71\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"AURORA\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8057}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"AURORA\",\"source_path\":\"sources/AURORA_AUTHORITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"debbe3de17dc0511fe3b9f5be920a83367c84efaedb34ef4095a9add315a0761\",\"source_size_bytes\":4111,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Emergency authority and restoration accountability\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe incident commander may isolate zones and order emergency work. Only the county health officer may lift a do-not-drink order, and only after current laboratory and distribution-system verification; a utility repair or green mechanical check is not public-health authorization.\nEmergency procurement does not waive operator certification, chain of custody, environmental permits, access control, or fiscal review. Final closure requires the utility director to accept every declared blocker and residual risk.\nA handoff is valid only when the receiving lead acknowledges the same hydraulic model, treatment train, sampling plan, pump configuration, and communication version. A version mismatch blocks closure.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nBASTION and CIPHER supply hydraulic and laboratory evidence but cannot lift health restrictions. NEXUS supplies independent readiness findings but does not execute restoration.\nMOSAIC owns rollback mechanics; AURORA preserves separation among detection, recommendation, authorization, execution, verification, communication, and closure.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| AUT-000 | incident-command | v2 | 1.0 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-001 | health-officer | v2 | 2.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-002 | utility-director | v2 | 3.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-003 | public-information | v2 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-004 | incident-command | v2 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-005 | health-officer | v2 | 1.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-006 | utility-director | v2 | 2.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-007 | public-information | v2 | 3.9 | approval | current |\n| AUT-008 | incident-command | v2 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-009 | health-officer | v2 | 3.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-010 | utility-director | v2 | 1.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-011 | public-information | v2 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n| AUT-012 | incident-command | v2 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-013 | health-officer | v2 | 2.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-014 | utility-director | v3 | 3.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-015 | public-information | v3 | 1.9 | approval | current |\n| AUT-016 | incident-command | v3 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-017 | health-officer | v3 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-018 | utility-director | v3 | 2.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-019 