1-64+DELTA:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"64721c48b86decba9adecca404e0e207db15cc1c0611470f2fe6e28207610bef\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-002\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8452}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"source_path\":\"sources/CIPHER_LAB.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"6db7f6a91d666ab9e013e147aa946885080f48117bd461c8a542171378aba4cb\",\"source_size_bytes\":3991,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Laboratory sampling, detection limits, and clearance evidence\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe current confirmatory set has zero E. coli positives across forty-eight samples. Clearance requires two complete rounds at least sixteen hours apart; one clean round is insufficient.\nThe benzene reporting limit is 0.5 micrograms per liter and the action threshold is 5.0 micrograms per liter. The reporting limit is not the action threshold and neither is a percent concentration.\nA flow-path, disinfectant-dose, source-water, sampling-plan, or laboratory-method change makes prior samples stale for the changed candidate.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCIPHER sample placement consumes BASTION flow paths and GARNET contamination hypotheses. HELIX governs chain of custody and laboratory access.\nAURORA consumes current CIPHER findings for advisory decisions; CIPHER does not itself authorize public restoration.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| LAB-000 | entry-point | v2 | 0.0 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-001 | north-grid | v2 | 1.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-002 | south-grid | v2 | 2.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-003 | hospital-loop | v2 | 0.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-004 | entry-point | v2 | 2.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-005 | north-grid | v2 | 0.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-006 | south-grid | v2 | 1.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-007 | hospital-loop | v2 | 2.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-008 | entry-point | v2 | 1.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-009 | north-grid | v2 | 2.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-010 | south-grid | v2 | 0.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-011 | hospital-loop | v2 | 1.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-012 | entry-point | v2 | 0.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-013 | north-grid | v2 | 1.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-014 | south-grid | v3 | 2.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-015 | hospital-loop | v3 | 0.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-016 | entry-point | v3 | 2.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-017 | north-grid | v3 | 0.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-018 | south-grid | v3 | 1.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-019 | hospital-loop | v3 | 3.0 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-020 | entry-point | v3 | 1.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-021 | north-grid | v3 | 2.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-022 | south-grid | v3 | 0.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-023 | hospital-loop | v3 | 2.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-024 | entry-point | v3 | 0.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-025 | north-grid | v3 | 1.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-026 | south-grid | v3 | 2.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-027 | hospital-loop | v3 | 1.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-028 | entry-point | v4 | 2.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-029 | north-grid | v4 | 0.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-030 | south-grid | v4 | 1.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-031 | hospital-loop | v4 | 0.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-032 | entry-point | v4 | 1.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-033 | north-grid | v4 | 2.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-034 | south-grid | v4 | 0.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-035 | hospital-loop | v4 | 2.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-036 | entry-point | v4 | 0.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-037 | north-grid | v4 | 1.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-038 | south-grid | v4 | 2.9 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-039 | hospital-loop | v4 | 1.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-040 | entry-point | v4 | 2.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-041 | north-grid | v4 | 0.6 | positive-samples | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve rounds, spacing, sample count, detection limit, action threshold, and staleness.\nState what negative result would falsify clearance and trigger renewed isolation.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"source_path\":\"sources/DELTA_PUMPS.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"4c3707d0d2ae07ceb2bda6d83cf6585510f5398db7c66568ba38aa3fd3f01169\",\"source_size_bytes\":4013,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Pump capacity, sequencing, and cavitation constraints\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe treatment works can supply 18 million gallons per day, but the shared transmission main is capped at 14.5 MGD. Pump nameplate capacities cannot be summed into usable system flow.\nThe latest inspected configuration sustained 12.8 MGD after fire-flow and hospital reserve. A higher stage requires a current candidate-bound pump and pressure test.\nRestoration may advance through 10, 30, 60, and 100 percent demand stages only after two thirty-minute windows meet pressure, turbidity, power, and storage gates.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nBASTION supplies pressure limits, ECHO supplies feeder headroom, and FALCON supplies treatment output. All three constrain DELTA sequencing.\nA pump, valve, main allocation, generator, or treatment-train change makes prior capacity evidence stale.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version 