ce_size_bytes\":3565,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Grid, generator, and fuel continuity\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe grid feed is rated at 8.2 MW, but the damaged switchgear limits current delivery to 6.5 MW. Rating and currently usable power must not be swapped.\nEmergency generation can carry 4.1 MW for thirty-six hours at the current fuel stock. The duration is not thirty-six days and excludes mobile-pump load.\nAutomatic transfer succeeded in the latest drill, but the observation predates switchgear version SW-9 and is stale for the current candidate.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nDELTA pump stages and FALCON treatment trains compete for ECHO capacity. KESTREL fuel delivery controls generator duration.\nINDIGO telemetry is required to validate voltage and transfer stability; a control-room display alone is insufficient.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| PWR-000 | substation-a | v2 | 6.5 | megawatts | superseded |\n| PWR-001 | substation-b | v2 | 7.8 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-002 | generator-1 | v2 | 9.1 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-003 | fuel-yard | v2 | 7.3 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-004 | substation-a | v2 | 8.6 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-005 | substation-b | v2 | 6.8 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-006 | generator-1 | v2 | 8.1 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-007 | fuel-yard | v2 | 9.4 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-008 | substation-a | v2 | 7.6 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-009 | substation-b | v2 | 8.9 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-010 | generator-1 | v2 | 7.1 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-011 | fuel-yard | v2 | 8.4 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-012 | substation-a | v2 | 6.6 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-013 | substation-b | v2 | 7.9 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-014 | generator-1 | v3 | 9.2 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-015 | fuel-yard | v3 | 7.4 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-016 | substation-a | v3 | 8.7 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-017 | substation-b | v3 | 6.9 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-018 | generator-1 | v3 | 8.2 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-019 | fuel-yard | v3 | 9.5 | megawatts | superseded |\n| PWR-020 | substation-a | v3 | 7.7 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-021 | substation-b | v3 | 9.0 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-022 | generator-1 | v3 | 7.2 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-023 | fuel-yard | v3 | 8.5 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-024 | substation-a | v3 | 6.7 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-025 | substation-b | v3 | 8.0 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-026 | generator-1 | v3 | 9.3 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-027 | fuel-yard | v3 | 7.5 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-028 | substation-a | v4 | 8.8 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-029 | substation-b | v4 | 7.0 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-030 | generator-1 | v4 | 8.3 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-031 | fuel-yard | v4 | 6.5 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-032 | substation-a | v4 | 7.8 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-033 | substation-b | v4 | 9.1 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-034 | generator-1 | v4 | 7.3 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-035 | fuel-yard | v4 | 8.6 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-036 | substation-a | v4 | 6.8 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-037 | substation-b | v4 | 8.1 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-038 | generator-1 | v4 | 9.4 | megawatts | superseded |\n| PWR-039 | fuel-yard | v4 | 7.6 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-040 | substation-a | v4 | 8.9 | megawatts | current |\n| PWR-041 | substation-b | v4 | 7.1 | megawatts | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nSeparate rated, usable, generated, and reserved power with exact durations.\nName current tests for transfer, load shedding, fuel replenishment, and rollback.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"FALCON\",\"source_path\":\"sources/FALCON_TREATMENT.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"62997706c361243e5d2720ccc088b53d3bcc2c64e64e6ee054d588aeac8fd8b8\",\"source_size_bytes\":3344,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Treatment barriers, disinfectant, and turbidity controls\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nCurrent combined-filter turbidity is 0.18 NTU. The release gate is at or below 0.30 NTU for four hours; 0.18 NTU is not a chlorine residual.\nFree chlorine must remain between 0.8 and 2.0 milligrams per liter at entry points and at least 0.2 mg/L in distribution. Entry and distribution thresholds are different controls.\nFilter media, coagulant dose, source-water blend, contact time, or UV configuration changes stale prior treatment verification.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nGARNET source-water findings set FALCON treatment assumptions. BASTION residence time and CIPHER sampling determine whether treated water evidence applies downstream.\nDELTA demand ramps cannot outrun FALCON verified capacity or required disinfectant contact time.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| TRT-000 | clarifier | v2 | 0.2 | ntu | superseded |\n| TRT-001 | filter-bank | v2 | 1.5 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-002 | chlorine-contact | v2 | 2.8 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-003 | uv-train | v2 | 1.0 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-004 | clarifier | v2 | 2.3 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-005 | filter-bank | v2 | 0.5 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-006 | chlorine-contact | v2 | 1.8 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-007 | uv-train | v2 | 3.1 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-008 | clarifier | v2 | 1.3 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-009 | filter-bank | v2 | 2.6 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-010 | chlorine-contact | v2 | 0.8 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-011 | uv-train | v2 | 2.1 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-012 | clarifier | v2 | 0.3 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-013 | filter-bank | v2 | 1.6 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-014 | chlorine-contact | v3 | 2.9 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-015 | uv-train | v3 | 1.1 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-016 | clarifier | v3 | 2.4 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-017 | filter-bank | v3 | 0.6 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-018 | chlorine-contact | v3 | 1.9 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-019 | uv-train | v3 | 3.2 | ntu | superseded |\n| TRT-020 | clarifier | v3 | 1.4 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-021 | filter-bank | v3 | 2.7 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-022 | chlorine-contact | v3 | 0.9 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-023 | uv-train | v3 | 2.2 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-024 | clarifier | v3 | 0.4 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-025 | filter-bank | v3 | 1.7 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-026 | chlorine-contact | v3 | 3.0 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-027 | uv-train | v3 | 1.2 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-028 | clarifier | v4 | 2.5 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-029 | filter-bank | v4 | 0.7 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-030 | chlorine-contact | v4 | 2.0 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-031 | uv-train | v4 | 0.2 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-032 | clarifier | v4 | 1.5 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-033 | filter-bank | v4 | 2.8 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-034 | chlorine-contact | v4 | 1.0 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-035 | uv-train | v4 | 2.3 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-036 | clarifier | v4 | 0.5 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-037 | filter-bank | v4 | 1.8 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-038 | chlorine-contact | v4 | 3.1 | ntu | superseded |\n| TRT-039 | uv-train | v4 | 1.3 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-040 | clarifier | v4 | 2.6 | ntu | current |\n| TRT-041 | filter-bank | v4 | 0.8 | ntu | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve NTU, mg/L, locations, duration, and barrier dependencies.\nState pause, rollback, and evidence needed to retire temporary treatment controls.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-004\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"result:RESULT-004\",\"object_version\":\"d5136d0f16c7b6393712bbe144f08434045e051ff1da61fedcf5588b28b60373\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-019\",\"result_kind\":\"exact_reopen_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"original_result_id\":\"RESULT-004\",\"original_sha256\":\"d5136d0f16c7b6393712bbe144f08434045e051ff1da61fedcf5588b28b60373\",\"schema\":\"architecture-exact-reopen-v0\"}\n--- exact original model-visible result ---\n{\"obje