05 | reservoir | v2 | 3.7 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-006 | ash-plume | v2 | 5.0 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-007 | chemical-yard | v2 | 6.3 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-008 | river-intake | v2 | 4.5 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-009 | reservoir | v2 | 5.8 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-010 | ash-plume | v2 | 4.0 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-011 | chemical-yard | v2 | 5.3 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-012 | river-intake | v2 | 3.5 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-013 | reservoir | v2 | 4.8 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-014 | ash-plume | v3 | 6.1 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-015 | chemical-yard | v3 | 4.3 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-016 | river-intake | v3 | 5.6 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-017 | reservoir | v3 | 3.8 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-018 | ash-plume | v3 | 5.1 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-019 | chemical-yard | v3 | 6.4 | risk-index | superseded |\n| SRC-020 | river-intake | v3 | 4.6 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-021 | reservoir | v3 | 5.9 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-022 | ash-plume | v3 | 4.1 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-023 | chemical-yard | v3 | 5.4 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-024 | river-intake | v3 | 3.6 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-025 | reservoir | v3 | 4.9 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-026 | ash-plume | v3 | 6.2 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-027 | chemical-yard | v3 | 4.4 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-028 | river-intake | v4 | 5.7 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-029 | reservoir | v4 | 3.9 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-030 | ash-plume | v4 | 5.2 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-031 | chemical-yard | v4 | 3.4 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-032 | river-intake | v4 | 4.7 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-033 | reservoir | v4 | 6.0 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-034 | ash-plume | v4 | 4.2 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-035 | chemical-yard | v4 | 5.5 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-036 | river-intake | v4 | 3.7 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-037 | reservoir | v4 | 5.0 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-038 | ash-plume | v4 | 6.3 | risk-index | superseded |\n| SRC-039 | chemical-yard | v4 | 4.5 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-040 | river-intake | v4 | 5.8 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-041 | reservoir | v4 | 4.0 | risk-index | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve forecast versus observation, percent versus concentration, and location.\nKeep the investigation hold until named inspection and sampling evidence retires it.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"HELIX\",\"source_path\":\"sources/HELIX_SECURITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"dcb5a4ce70bf47372c5a52a096e89f890c74f7be1363fd78dfaf9c6cd10536e5\",\"source_size_bytes\":3386,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Access, control-system integrity, and evidence custody\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe exposed SCADA service token was revoked at 14:10 UTC. The controller signing key was not exposed and remains current under key-set version W4.\nBreak-glass access expires after two hours and requires dual approval plus immutable session logging. Emergency access is not continuing authorization.\nOnline control logs are retained for ninety days and archived incident evidence for seven years; the periods serve different obligations.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nAURORA governs emergency authority and MOSAIC binds rollback to the current key set. INDIGO consumes HELIX audit events but does not authorize access.\nAny key-set, role-policy, controller, or logging mutation makes prior security verification stale.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| SEC-000 | scada-token | v2 | 2.0 | hours | superseded |\n| SEC-001 | operator-role | v2 | 3.3 | hours | current |\n| SEC-002 | lab-chain | v2 | 4.6 | hours | current |\n| SEC-003 | audit-log | v2 | 2.8 | hours | current |\n| SEC-004 | scada-token | v2 | 4.1 | hours | current |\n| SEC-005 | operator-role | v2 | 2.3 | hours | current |\n| SEC-006 | lab