 38.4 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-041 | chlorine | v4 | 36.6 | hours-cover | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve load regime, stock type, days versus hours, staffing time, and uncertainty.\nName reorder triggers, alternates, owner, and retirement evidence.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"LUMEN\",\"source_path\":\"sources/LUMEN_PUBLIC.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"1a50bae39974b3c33c2a0a6b6b94859b75f41e3c4d4a01f17cf519db7b98253c\",\"source_size_bytes\":3813,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Public warnings, accessibility, and customer continuity\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nDo-not-drink notices reached 91 percent of registered endpoints; the missing nine percent is communication uncertainty, not a nine-percent reduction in affected population.\nPublic states must distinguish do-not-use, do-not-drink, boil-water, restricted service, and cleared. Low pressure does not by itself establish contamination.\nThe call center can sustain 3,200 contacts per hour for six hours. Forecast demand is 4,100 per hour unless alternate-language outreach reduces repeat calls.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCIPHER and AURORA determine advisory status; INDIGO and BASTION supply service observations. HELIX constrains publication of sensitive infrastructure details.\nJASPER supplies mandatory environmental language and KESTREL supplies verified alternate-water locations.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| COM-000 | sms | v2 | 91.0 | percent-delivered | superseded |\n| COM-001 | radio | v2 | 92.3 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-002 | clinics | v2 | 93.6 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-003 | schools | v2 | 91.8 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-004 | sms | v2 | 93.1 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-005 | radio | v2 | 91.3 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-006 | clinics | v2 | 92.6 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-00